('phantom_fungus','Phantom Fungus','Phantom Fungus','3','Medium','Plant','Always neutral','2d8+6 (15 hp)',15,'+0','20 ft. (4 squares)','14 (+4 natural), touch 10, flat-footed 14','+1/+3','Bite +3 melee (1d6+3)','5 ft./5 ft.','+6','+0','+0',14,10,16,2,11,9,'Listen +4, Move Silently +6, Spot +4','Alertness','{"special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, plant traits, greater invisibility"}'::jsonb,'This creature looks like a brown and greenish-brown mass with a cluster of nodules atop the main mass, though it is visible only when dead. A cluster of nodules atop the main mass serve as sensory organs. The creature feeds and attacks with a gaping maw lined with rows of teeth. Four stumpy legs support the creature and allow it to move about. This ambulatory fungus is naturally invisible, making it a feared predator among subterranean inhabitants.','{"full_attack":"Bite +3 melee (1d6+3)","statblock":{"hit_dice":"2d8+6 (15 hp)","hit_points":15,"base_attack_grapple":"+1/+3","attack":"Bite +3 melee (1d6+3)","full_attack":"Bite +3 melee (1d6+3)","space_reach":"5 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +6, Ref +0, Will +0","abilities":{"str":"14","dex":"10","con":"16","int":"2","wis":"11","cha":"9"},"skills":"Listen +4, Move Silently +6, Spot +4","feats":"Alertness","special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, plant traits, greater invisibility"},"source_file":"monsters-o-r.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-o-r.html',true),
